Notebook[{
Cell["WolframExample: Rust libraries from the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"f3f89738-df89-46c6-98b8-bd90f0ce6efc"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook exercises the WolframExample paclet, whose functions are \
implemented in Rust (see WolframExample/Libs). Evaluate it top to bottom.

If the setup section reports a missing paclet, build the library first:
    cd WolframExample && cargo wl build\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40d84826-7693-49ba-aa55-0da6b8056bca"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0f4531b7-9e8c-47a7-ad5f-94b3ef49eaf1"],

Cell["\<\
Both paclets \[LongDash] the hand-written WolframExample and the generated \
WolframExampleLib \[LongDash] sit in this notebook's parent directory, so one \
PacletDirectoryLoad registers both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38b4bc95-d7eb-4245-b7dc-f495844d7134"],

Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d8d5133c-1a1e-4d14-9947-af765553f78f"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExample\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4de69b23-943f-4fd6-af34-68e1ea250aab"],

Cell["\<\
The library paclet holds nothing but the compiled dylibs and a generated \
Functions.wl loader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60cd8222-afbc-4404-82f4-981c0ddec885"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"eac9a03f-21e0-4f45-b32b-00b93e8ebe26"],

Cell["Needs[\"WolframExample`\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"50aa3318-1adb-47f0-8dda-db5aa9dab3ed"],

Cell["Everything the package exports:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41bcce97-ee7f-4bac-af5b-924007de97f3"],

Cell["?WolframExample`*", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"04d873b3-9d69-4994-a9f9-53d257bb87a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e23efa99-ff84-4d90-9591-67d7cce5bbe5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scalars and arrays", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e21e8ab6-369e-4c9d-b667-8b1e14711aa0"],

Cell["\<\
A plain Rust function over two f64s. Arguments and result cross as raw \
MArgument scalars \[LongDash] no serialization at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4e4cb76-b100-4291-a875-44ab639bbdce"],

Cell["ExampleAdd[2, 3]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"10459607-fecf-4aed-837f-196df8a2007a"],

Cell["\<\
NumericArrays are read zero-copy: Rust sees the kernel's own memory, no copy \
and no conversion. Lists are packed into a Real64 NumericArray by the wrapper \
first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e734a82-b7e2-4b7d-85c7-35fb0a1fe88b"],

Cell["ExampleDot[{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ce1a6361-6af4-4f82-82e6-d9e51c1c188c"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleDot[
    NumericArray[Range[1., 100000.], \"Real64\"],
    NumericArray[Range[100000., 1., -1.], \"Real64\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"25d39d70-6d7a-4130-baa8-fb1e5a982e46"],

Cell["\<\
The Rust side accumulates into 8 independent lanes so that LLVM can vectorize \
the loop (see Libs/math/src/lib.rs) \[LongDash] about twice the throughput of \
the naive left-to-right sum. Timed against the kernel's own Dot, which calls \
into BLAS; a Speedup above 1 means the Rust library won.

Two things decide what you see here. Time only the call, not the packing: \
both arrays are converted to NumericArrays first, since passing plain lists \
spends about three times the call itself on the conversion. And build with    \
 cargo wl build --release
\[LongDash] cargo wl test leaves an unoptimized build in place, which loses \
by an order of magnitude.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9168a20e-bcbb-4dbb-9f3a-eb6a68b9c2df"],

Cell["\<\
With[
    {a = Range[1., 100000.], b = Range[100000., 1., -1.]},
    {na = NumericArray[a, \"Real64\"], nb = NumericArray[b, \"Real64\"]},
    {rust = First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[na, nb],
     kernel = First @ RepeatedTiming @ Dot[a, b],
     packing = First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[a, b]},
    <|
        \"Rust\" -> Quantity[rust, \"Seconds\"],
        \"Kernel\" -> Quantity[kernel, \"Seconds\"],
        \"Speedup\" -> kernel / rust,
        \"RustFromLists\" -> Quantity[packing, \"Seconds\"]
    |>
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"edb142c8-eddb-4502-9fbe-0505af249b98"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structs and enums", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d6a671ba-c357-425a-b72d-7fc8066e7b02"],

Cell["\<\
Structured arguments cross as WXF. A Rust struct is an Association keyed by \
its field names; the wrapper here presents Wolfram-style capitalized keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f3a8fb2-2d27-4060-bf16-b40bc067427b"],

Cell["ExampleSymmetricPoint[<|\"X\" -> 10, \"Y\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0f09a3a2-a84e-4d8d-b788-ca24a7723b46"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleArea goes through a Rust enum \[LongDash] one function, one match, two \
shapes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"854610b7-7bb6-40e5-9a65-320aca09dff7"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> 1|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bfa767ba-5889-4a16-a74e-b4ff2f79387d"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Width\" -> 10, \"Height\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"21465d08-e0ee-4dbe-9908-137e43c7d7bc"],

Cell["Table[ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> r|>], {r, 1, 5}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2ac673b7-6d2e-4db2-ab5e-440409c3b859"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Errors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6fe0528b-573f-4481-8589-99ff4daeff1f"],

Cell["\<\
A Rust Result<f64, String> comes back as {\"Ok\", value} or {\"Err\", \
message}; the wrapper turns the error branch into a Failure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d152257-f6b0-427b-9365-a6bd7527d495"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[10, 4]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2afabdf9-1a5a-4117-aa31-f43a8d3e2d87"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7736c1a5-46c7-4240-a34d-24b9afbc39b2"],

Cell["So the usual Failure handling applies:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f0fb48c8-a781-4708-8476-46bc43e44452"],

Cell["\<\
FailureQ /@ {ExampleSafeDivide[1, 2], ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b2eec311-75f0-46e7-b268-a2d33b6ea47c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["DuckDB", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9ad978ba-28df-44c4-a70a-bc3b120ff06d"],

Cell["\<\
An entire embedded SQL engine, statically linked into the library \[LongDash] \
nothing to install. Query results come back as Arrow and are decoded into a \
Tabular.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e62eb530-e788-4aa9-8ac7-4a385b69d23b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scoped connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6aaefdea-44a2-42af-aad2-8a3e0590bb82"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute opens a connection, applies the function to it, and closes it \
again \[LongDash] even if the body fails.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60a92515-8826-4235-88de-58994b6aff22"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT 42 AS answer\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"61cc0ef7-eee0-4d12-a7a0-de231f8a69bf"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n::INTEGER AS id,
            (n * 1.5)::DOUBLE AS score,
            'item_' || n AS label,
            n % 2 = 0 AS is_even
     FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n)\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e27d04bd-b159-4b30-bd7a-8ab88430c35c"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an ordinary Tabular, so the usual operations work:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0a1774a-9524-4727-9ef8-29d10c565127"],

Cell["\<\
tab = DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 100) t(n)\"] &];
{Length[tab], Total[tab[[All, \"n\"]]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cf6cd9ac-bb57-4a8c-bef8-0b6f396f615f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f835839f-6b5f-4a33-b91b-a3540f0e5367"],

Cell["\<\
Values are bound to the ? placeholders in order, so nothing is interpolated \
into the SQL string.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d3e6fc6-37ea-48bb-967d-c9a93e9c765f"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n) WHERE n > ?\", {2}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3cba923c-27eb-4f1f-b01f-557ae59918ab"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT ?::INTEGER + ?::INTEGER AS total\", {20, 22}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dc6cdad0-4b03-401e-b74b-8e98892c2995"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explicit connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"08f3a300-083f-49b8-b3d4-5d9de32b4c17"],

Cell["\<\
For several statements against the same database, hold the handle yourself. \
Here an on-disk file, which persists after disconnecting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ceabd492-de79-4e0a-8e84-02bf45444b5c"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"wolfram-example.duckdb\"}];
Quiet[DeleteFile[file]];
conn = DuckDBConnect[\"duckdb:///\" <> file]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4b422570-b625-44e5-b2fc-3db22d76ef7e"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn,
    \"CREATE TABLE fruit AS SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'apple'), (2, 'pear')) \
v(id, name)\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fe23cfa6-ce21-4aed-8c60-a895adce4650"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn, \"INSERT INTO fruit VALUES (?, ?)\", {3, \"plum\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"852c02f8-cf8e-4a68-b10a-e17baca4047b"],

Cell["DuckDBQuery[conn, \"SELECT * FROM fruit ORDER BY id\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"92e8be63-490a-45a7-9b5f-3bff8b757150"],

Cell["DuckDBDisconnect[conn]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"858ceeac-0e70-43d2-adc8-9eeea117d1ec"],

Cell["Reopening the same file shows the rows are still there:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e34310b3-eff1-4661-8bac-13c91626e208"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb:///\" <> file,
    DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT count(*) AS rows FROM fruit\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c23a817e-b054-4790-9c8d-84cc94badc51"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Failures", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"26da5501-60ae-4d83-9339-645f1b1e03e1"],

Cell["\<\
Errors from the engine arrive as Failure objects carrying DuckDB's own \
message, and propagate on their own.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b695c8b9-1ce2-4c0a-a0a3-686d4fba460c"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT * FROM no_such_table\"] \
&]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2b1d782c-621f-4894-a783-35a5740ccb4a"],

Cell["\<\
A handle that has been closed is no longer in the Rust-side registry:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb4fb165-192c-4487-a395-6776e8a367a0"],

Cell["\<\
With[{c = DuckDBConnect[]},
    DuckDBDisconnect[c];
    DuckDBQuery[c, \"SELECT 1\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9db460ca-717a-4c5b-8a00-b6277097d45f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The raw library", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b1a2e96-7836-4927-9616-caa8aeeda4b3"],

Cell["\<\
The wrappers in Kernel/WolframExample.wl are a thin layer over an association \
of LibraryFunctions, keyed \"namespace::rust_name\". Anything without a \
wrapper is still one lookup away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21129fe6-f709-40e4-95ca-192c04fa1bba"],

Cell["Keys[WolframExampleFunctions[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"79f0f90a-80b2-4b80-893b-1dd2ec6ec373"],

Cell["\<\
inactive_sum builds an expression in Rust and returns it unevaluated:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc5e9eb2-80f4-45f1-844f-5a71e5f8f8a6"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2572455c-914e-4d4b-a583-49baff74197a"],

Cell["\<\
Activate[WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ed8a66ff-74ca-4169-866a-7b4354db937e"],

Cell["\<\
A panic on the Rust side is caught at the boundary and returned as a Failure \
\[LongDash] it does not take the kernel down:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dcea7a99-1194-40c7-b541-4b6771d0ed10"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::panic\"][]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"66015c1d-dfe5-4633-8e26-26754b28aec0"],

Cell["\<\
And the signatures of everything that was packaged, straight from the \
generated Artifacts.wl asset:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18f86e03-171e-465f-928e-1d7efc274b96"],

Cell["\<\
Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \"Artifacts\"]] //
    Map[Query[{\"Name\", \"Signatures\"}]] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0ca662bd-dc0a-4004-80c0-ed078003abd0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rebuilding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cb1a2e17-3bf3-48aa-a888-ed729943dcda"],

Cell["\<\
After editing the Rust source, rebuild from the paclet directory. The dylibs \
are content-hashed, so a rebuilt library gets a new file name \[LongDash] \
quit the kernel to pick it up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90beeb01-85e2-4113-a33d-6be5fe6cba80"],

Cell["\<\
ExternalEvaluate[{\"Shell\",
    \"ProcessDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"WolframExample\"}],
    \"ProcessEnvironment\" -> <|\"PATH\" -> Environment[\"PATH\"]|>},
   \"cargo wl build --release\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"76b5cda0-969f-45d1-98e2-73ea7c53dbad"]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowTitle->"WolframExample Tour",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 6, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"ff380777-6ac3-4c38-b635-0db2def3f088"
]
